<h2 id="inspect-the-achievement-behind-the-image">Inspect the achievement behind the image</h2>

<p>The <a href="https://www.imsglobal.org/spec/ob/v3p0/">Open Badges 3.0 specification</a> describes achievement credentials, not just decorative images. Inspect issuer, recipient association, achievement, criteria, evidence, dates and supported proof. A university workshop attendance badge and an assessed laboratory milestone should not claim the same capability.</p>

<p>A laboratory milestone names the assessed task and an authorized evidence reference. Proof checking supports integrity; the receiver still evaluates issuer authority and the assessment. For the deeper institution-focused explanation, use <a href="/blog/why-institutions-should-embrace-open-badges-3-0-standards">Open Badges governance</a>. For the verification mechanics and resource dependencies, use the <a href="/blog/Understanding-W3C-Verifiable-Credentials.html">W3C guide</a>.</p>
